  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF THE TIGERS OF BUKIT BARISAN SELATAN THROUGH IMPROVED LAW ENFORCEMENT AND REDUCED HUMAN-TIGER CONFLICT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The long term goal of this project is to bring tigers back to their natural carrying capacity in Bukit Barisan Selatan (BBS) National Park and to bring the tiger population of Bukit Balai Rejang (BBR) to a level that is both capable of sustained breeding and compatible with the human activities legally permitted within BBR. This is to be done through improving and strengthening law enforcement and human-tiger conflict mitigation in the BBS/BBR landscape. Project objectives include: (1) Decrease poaching of tigers; (2) Decrease killing of tiger prey; (3) Decrease rate of deforestation; and, (4) Decrease human-tiger conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
